    "body": "<!-- crb-followup-result:v1 harvest=934 -->\n### Triage result\n\nEpic: #935\n\n- #936 [followups-934 01/07] Remove dead code from three data-package tests\n- #937 [followups-934 02/07] Check the affected-row count of three unchecked targeted updates\n- #938 [followups-934 03/07] Replace five unchecked boundary casts with runtime checks\n- #939 [followups-934 04/07] Close six test coverage gaps flagged by the review bot\n- #940 [followups-934 05/07] Narrow three failure paths that over-report or over-swallow\n- #941 [followups-934 06/07] Remove a redundant retry status and fix three stale or ungrammatical texts\n- #942 [followups-934 07/07] Constrain the arguments of the failEventsFor test helper\n\n#### Rejected (2)\n\n| PR | Key | Verdict | Reason | Tracked by |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #778 | 8abe5b9661 | already-fixed | Migration was renumbered 0052->0053 (pathExists false); the unique index is now ON mail_message_meta (message_id, mailbox_item_id) with the explaining comment at lines 70-75, as the thread replies (4feec10) claim and the code confirms. (backend/packages/data/src/db/migrations/0053_mail_message_meta_per_mailbox.sql:77) |  |\n| #845 | a8b32415cf | already-fixed | Commit 37649e9b closes the agent_runs row and its run_status event atomically (closeAtomically); the error path writes the only terminal event when the close fails, so done+error can no longer both be committed. Tracked in #853 as the thread says. (backend/packages/agent-runtime/src/lifecycleAdapter.ts:158) |  |\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=778 key=8abe5b9661 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=845 key=a8b32415cf -->\n\n#### Advisories\n\nNone.\n",
